{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>You have declared HaShem this day, and HaShem has declared you.</b> It was stated in the first chapter of Berakhot: the Holy One, blessed be He, said: You have hewn Me into one block in the world, in that you say ״שמע ישראל ה' אלהינו ה' אחד״, and I will make you into one block in the world, as it is said: ״מי כעמך ישראל גוי אחד בארץ״. Another interpretation: האמרת — an expression of exchange and substitution, that is: for the sake of HaShem you exchanged all other divinities and chose the Holy One, blessed be He; and וה' האמירך — He exchanged all the nations of the world and chose you to be for Him a treasured people. And so may all doers of iniquity be likened — who exchange their words and do not stand by their word. Another interpretation: an expression of amir and branch, which is an expression of height, as it is written: ״שנים שלשה גרגרים בראש אמיר״ — and here, את ה' האמרת — you elevated Him above all gods; וה' האמירך — He elevated you above all the nations. And so may all doers of iniquity be likened — who elevate themselves out of the gross arrogance within them. And I have heard that in the Jerusalem Targum it is translated האמרת — המלכת (you enthroned), for in the Arabic tongue a king is called amir."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:01:26.316737502Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}